    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f98401b8_cec06220",
        "filename": "java/framework/src/android/system/virtualmachine/VirtualMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 444,
      "author": {
        "id": 1897307
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-02T16:44:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e This should probably be extracted to a (non-static) method on VirtualMachine.\n\n\nWouldn\u0027t that require an additional api \u0026 be in scope of api changes then?\n\nAlso, currently the claiming of VM instance is hidden in a way. Instance-id (or instance.img) are under the hood implementation details.\n\nSo if we extract out this into `VirtualMachine::claimInstance()`, it increases 1 step in claiming the VM. What if the user does `fromDescriptor` but not claimInstance().  It is seems the only sensible place to call `VirtualMachine::claimInstance` is after constructing VM from a descriptor \u0026 the current code achieves it?",
      "parentUuid": "1d95b485_4581c361",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 436,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 444,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "9a57cede122cd1658a5cd1790ee670826e8d7719",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "43740747_1948a326",
        "filename": "java/framework/src/android/system/virtualmachine/VirtualMachine.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 444,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-03T08:54:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Only public methods are part of the API; we\u0027re free to add private (or in this case probably package protected) methods, and only we can call them.\n\nI\u0027m not suggesting we change the visible API at all; just some light refactoring. \n\nThis looks like a method on a VM - all those `vm.` accesses gives it away (\"feature envy\"). And if we do extract it, it then becomes easy to move outside the lock, which seems like a win. (The lock is there to protect the consistency of which VMs exist, in the file system and in the in-memory map. Claiming an instance ID doesn\u0027t affect either.)",
      "parentUuid": "f98401b8_cec06220",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 436,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 444,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "9a57cede122cd1658a5cd1790ee670826e8d7719",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
